 *   **Limitations:** Order confusion caused by overlap among cells is a potential issue, addressed by the calibration scalar $v_n$ [S1].
 *   **When to use:** When real-time rendering of Gaussian Splatting is required with high visual fidelity, specifically avoiding transparency and popping artifacts common in sort-free OIT methods [S1].
-*   **When not to use:** If strict per-Gaussian depth ordering is required for specific physical effects not covered by the cell-level approximation [S1].
 
 ## Background
-Duplex-GS was introduced in the paper "Duplex-GS: Proxy-Guided Weighted Blending for Real-Time Order-Independent Gaussian Splatting" [S1]. It builds upon Scaffold-GS [20] which introduced anchors as local encoding proxies. Duplex-GS replaces point anchors with ellipsoidal cells to provide explicit geometric structure [S1]. It addresses limitations of vanilla OIT-based Gaussian Splatting [16] which lacks physical constraints and causes transparency artifacts [S1].
